/*
To run on Windows:

1. Open Visual Studio.
2. Clone a repository. Fill in Repository Location and Path.
3. Click "Clone".

Chances are, you need to modify settings to get the program to work. First do step 1. 
Then, try to build and run the solution (At the top menu, click Build -> Clean Solution -> Rebuild Solution. If no errors, click Local Windows Debugger).
If there are errors, check your settings by doing steps 2 through 6 for each indicated project (bulleted under each step).

1. Right click solution -> Properties -> Common Properties -> Configure Startup Projects -> Single startup project = phase3_controller

2. Right click project -> Properties -> Configuration Properties -> Debugging -> Command Arguments = input dll output temp
- phase3_controller

3. Right click project -> Properties -> Configuration Properties -> General -> Output Directory = $(SolutionDir)bin\
Right click project -> Properties -> Configuration Properties -> Debugging -> Working Directory = $(SolutionDir)
- phase3_controller (main EXE) - makes sure relative paths like input, output, temp work correctly
- mapper_worker
- reducer_worker

4. Right click project -> Properties -> Configuration Properties -> General -> Output Directory = $(SolutionDir)dll\
Right click project -> Properties -> Configuration Properties -> Debugging -> Working Directory = $(SolutionDir)
- mapper_dll
- reducer_dll

5. Right click project -> Properties -> Configuration Properties -> General -> Intermediate Directory = $(SolutionDir)build\$(ProjectName)\
- mapper_dll
- mapper_worker
- phase3_controller
- reducer_dll
- reducer_worker

6. Right click project -> Properties -> Configuration Properties -> C/C++ -> General -> Additional Include Directories = $(SolutionDir)headers
- mapper_dll
- mapper_worker
- phase3_controller
- reducer_dll
- reducer_worker

*/
